---
import { links } from '../data/site';
const rules = [
  ['offer a branch as safe', 'git confirms its commits are already in the default branch, or a pull request merged them.'],
  ['offer a worktree as safe', 'it has no uncommitted changes and no commits that exist nowhere else.'],
  ['clear a generated folder', 'it is git-ignored, it is not a symlink, and it is checked again right before it moves to the Trash.'],
  ['remove anything at all', 'you reviewed the list and confirmed it.'],
  ['delete for good', 'it is something Lopper itself moved to the Trash, and you asked for it.'],
];
---
<section class="safety" id="safety" aria-labelledby="safety-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="safety-head">
      <h2 id="safety-title" class="title safety-title" data-scale-in>it never removes work that exists nowhere else.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        That is the whole job. Every rule below is covered by tests that run against real git repositories, because mocking git
        would hide exactly the cases that lose work. If Lopper cannot prove something is merged, it says so and leaves the
        decision to you.
      </p>
    </div>

    <dl class="ledger" aria-label="When Lopper acts">
      {rules.map(([what, when]) => (
        <div class="row" data-ledger-row>
          <span class="rule-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <dt><span class="will">Lopper will</span> {what}</dt>
          <dd><span class="only">only when</span> {when}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>

    <p class="safety-foot">
      Two independent reviewers audited every destructive path and a stress run measured 200 repositories.
      <a class="link" href={links.safety}>How it is checked, and what the audit found</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .safety { position: relative; z-index: 2; overflow-x: clip; background: #0d1412; padding-block: clamp(110px, 14vw, 200px); }
  .safety::before { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 0 0 auto; height: 240px; background: linear-gradient(var(--ink), transparent); pointer-events: none; }
  .safety-head { position: relative; display: grid; gap: 28px; max-width: 64rem; }
  .safety-title { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6.2vw, 6rem); max-width: 12em; }
  .safety-head .lead { max-width: 40rem; }

  .ledger { margin: clamp(64px, 9vw, 120px) 0 0; }
  .safety-foot { margin: 36px 0 0; max-width: 40rem; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--muted); }
  .safety-foot a { margin-left: 4px; }
  .row { position: relative; display: grid; gap: 10px; padding: 28px 0 30px; }
  .rule-line { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 0; height: 1px; background: var(--line-strong); transform-origin: 0 50%; }
  .row:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-strong); }
  .row dt { font-weight: 800; font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.6vw, 2.3rem); line-height: 1.05; letter-spacing: -0.025em; text-transform: lowercase; }
  .will { display: block; font: 500 0.85rem/1.6 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: 0; text-transform: none; color: var(--faint); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .row dd { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1.4vw, 1.3rem); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--muted); max-width: 34rem; }
  .only { display: block; font: 500 0.85rem/1.6 var(--font-mono); color: var(--mint); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .row { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 48px; align-items: start; padding: 34px 0 38px; }
  }
</style>
